// What the checker records for an editor (todo.md, Language server), as `ctxc decls` prints it.
// Each local's name is in scope from where it takes effect to the end of its scope: a
// context field's in the whole body, a let's after its statement, a pattern's binders in
// their arm or after the let-else, a narrowed view after the `if` that narrows it, and an
// `is` binder on the right of `and` and in the branch. Bodies checked twice record once.
//# build text: {home}/tests/helpers/text.ctx

// `ctxc decls` prints std's declarations too, thousands of lines that change with std, so the
// output isn't stated whole: its `live` lines are these, in a row,
//# $ ctxc decls {std:abs} -- main.ctx
//# stdout has:
//|
//| live s Shape main.ctx:3:38-13:2
//| live o ?i32 main.ctx:3:38-13:2
//| live k i32 main.ctx:4:14-13:2
//| live extra i32 main.ctx:5:52-13:2
//| live r i32 main.ctx:7:24-7:48
//| live side i32 main.ctx:8:27-11:10
//| live a i32 main.ctx:9:32-11:10
//| live s Shape main.ctx:15:40-24:2
//| live o ?i32 main.ctx:15:40-24:2
//| live o i32 main.ctx:16:30-24:2
//| live y i32 main.ctx:17:18-24:2
//| live r i32 main.ctx:18:29-18:34
//| live r i32 main.ctx:18:35-18:47
//| live t i32 main.ctx:20:18-22:6
//|

